# Intergrax — env config & vendor qualification

**Authority (semantic detail):** [`PLATFORM_ENTERPRISE_COMPLETION_ROADMAP.md`](../../docs/project/maintainers/plans/PLATFORM_ENTERPRISE_COMPLETION_ROADMAP.md), [`PLATFORM_ENTERPRISE_FREEZE_ACCEPTANCE_CHECKLIST.md`](../../docs/project/maintainers/qualification/PLATFORM_ENTERPRISE_FREEZE_ACCEPTANCE_CHECKLIST.md) (`FRZ-*`), [`VENDOR_BACKEND_NEUTRALITY_AND_REPLACEABILITY_EVIDENCE.md`](../../docs/project/maintainers/qualification/VENDOR_BACKEND_NEUTRALITY_AND_REPLACEABILITY_EVIDENCE.md). **Evidence layout:** [intergrax-session-artifacts.mdc](intergrax-session-artifacts.mdc) (`.tmp/` only).

## Environment configuration

- Environment-specific values **must** enter through **environment variables** and existing **approved typed configuration contracts** (Integrations/platform settings modules — not ad-hoc literals in product code).
- **Forbidden:** hardcoded credentials, API keys, secrets, or production vendor endpoints in source, tests committed as qualification proof, or agent/session artifacts.
- **Missing mandatory configuration:** fail closed at composition/startup — no silent defaults that widen authority or bypass contracts.
- **Diagnostic overrides:** explicit operator intent, temporary, isolated (prefer `.tmp/session/<task-id>/` overlays), restored after use; never checked into tracked trees.
- **Logging & evidence:** no secrets in logs, subprocess argv, process-tree snapshots, or qualification bundles; redact or omit — see session-artifacts rule for capture paths.

## Vendor integration qualification

- Prefer **Docker / Testcontainers** for real infrastructure when suitable: **pinned** service versions, readiness probes, bounded teardown.
- **Cloud-only** integrations: use controlled vendor **sandbox** environments when live integration proof is required.
- **Contract stubs, fakes, or in-process doubles** are not real vendor integration evidence — label scope accordingly in qualification records.
- Preserve **platform-defined contracts**, provider **replaceability**, and **sanctioned composition ownership** (`FRZ-CTR-*`, `FRZ-OWN-*`, `FRZ-BND-*` in freeze checklist); no vendor-specific shortcuts at semantic boundaries (`intergrax/` ↔ `agents/` ↔ `applications/` layering unchanged).

## Current C10/C15 restriction (operator freeze)

Until explicitly lifted by operator roadmap/qualification update — **do not change**:

- Preserve the **original Windows** execution environment for this workstream.
- **No Docker migration**, **no new vendor integrations**, **no production configuration** changes.
- **Diagnostic pytest** (broad/unbounded suites, harness replay): requires **separate operator authorization**; respect [intergrax-test-process-budget.mdc](intergrax-test-process-budget.mdc).
- **R7-Q**, **PROD-Q**, and global **`FRZ-*` statuses** remain unchanged by Cursor rule or tooling edits alone — gate plan: [`PROD_Q_R1_R7_Q_QUALIFICATION_INVENTORY_AND_GATE_PLAN.md`](../../docs/project/maintainers/qualification/PROD_Q_R1_R7_Q_QUALIFICATION_INVENTORY_AND_GATE_PLAN.md).
